@*
 * FILE ROLE: Runs before every view in this folder (and sub-folders) to set
 *            common properties — most importantly Layout, which names the
 *            shared _Layout.cshtml shell that wraps each view's content.
 *
 * SECTIONS IN THIS FILE:
 *   1. Layout assignment — how _ViewStart selects the default layout
 *
 * HOW _ViewStart.cshtml WORKS:
 *   Like _ViewImports.cshtml, the Razor engine walks the folder tree and
 *   executes every _ViewStart.cshtml it encounters before rendering a view.
 *   Inner-folder _ViewStart files run AFTER the outer one, so a Views/Admin/
 *   _ViewStart can override Layout for just the Admin section.
 *
 *   The code block here runs in the same context as the view, so the Layout
 *   property is the same Layout that can be overridden inside any view with:
 *       @{ Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_CustomLayout.cshtml"; }
 *   or suppressed entirely:
 *       @{ Layout = null; }
 *
 * WHAT BELONGS HERE:
 *   Only code that should run before EVERY view — typically just Layout = "...".
 *   Avoid business logic; this is a configuration entry-point, not a controller.
 *@

@*
 * SECTION 1: DEFAULT LAYOUT ASSIGNMENT
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Layout is a string property on the view's base class (RazorPage).
 * Setting it here means every view automatically uses _Layout.cshtml as its
 * outer HTML shell without needing to repeat the assignment in each file.
 *
 * PATH CONVENTIONS:
 *   "_Layout"            — Razor searches /Views/Shared/ and /Views/ (relative)
 *   "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml" — absolute virtual path from app root (~/);
 *                           safest form to avoid ambiguity in complex layouts
 *
 * HOW LAYOUT NESTING WORKS (RenderBody / RenderSection):
 *   _Layout.cshtml calls @RenderBody() where the view's HTML is inserted.
 *   Optional sections can be declared with @RenderSection("name", required:false)
 *   and filled from views with @section name { ... }.
 *   Detail in → Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml
 *@
@{
    Layout = "_Layout";   // resolves to Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml
}
